<title>USA: TVA Watts Bar nuke seen restarting Tuesday.</title>
<headline>TVA Watts Bar nuke seen restarting Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>TVA Nuclear's 1,170 megawatt (MW) Watts Bar unit is expected to restart Tuesday after tripping off line early Thursday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Spring City, Tenn., automatically shut down Thursday morning &quot;due to a broken shaft on the main feed pump,&quot; the NRC report stated.</p>
<p>As a matter of policy, TVA declines to comment on the status of its nuclear power plants.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
